1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:10,477
Welcome to the commissioning platform for the HD trackers at the Lagoinha solar plant. In this video, we walk through the executive view and how to use the platform.

2
00:00:11,967 --> 00:00:19,540
Each row is shown in the color of its current stage. The legend on the left explains every color; on mobile, tap “Legend”.

3
00:00:21,033 --> 00:00:30,335
The first tab gathers what matters for decision-making. The “Daily summary” turns the numbers into one sentence: progress, pace and forecast completion.

4
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:46,148
Separate bars show total, mechanical and electrical inspection progress. Below them, cards show commissioning, open non-conformities, deviation from the H D plan, the fifteen-day observation, and materials in shortage.

5
00:00:47,633 --> 00:00:56,039
Tap the i button next to each title to see what the indicator shows and how it is calculated. The cards open the detail tab.

6
00:00:57,533 --> 00:01:08,797
This chart shows where the flow is stuck. Many rows awaiting signatures point to a signature bottleneck. Many rows under correction point to an execution bottleneck on the H D side.

7
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:18,855
Compare the four areas, LAG one to LAG four, and follow weekly output. A drop in pace signals a delay in completion.

8
00:01:20,367 --> 00:01:27,769
An automatic list of what needs a decision or follow-up, with the owner of the next action. Click to open the related tab.

9
00:01:29,267 --> 00:01:38,248
In the Help tab you will find the guided tour, this video, a step-by-step guide for each role, the meaning of every color, and frequently asked questions.

10
00:01:39,733 --> 00:01:51,573
Each row follows the same flow: inspection, H D signature, C G N validation, correction, fifteen business days of observation, and finally commissioning with four signatures.

11
00:01:53,067 --> 00:02:06,592
Inspectors: open the inspection, mark each item as compliant, non-compliant or not applicable, and record measurements and photos. For each non-conformity, describe the condition found before any adjustment.

12
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:19,215
H D technicians: correct only what has been released, whether mechanical, electrical or both. Record a description and a photo, then tap: attest, resolved and OK.

13
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:29,724
C G N inspectors: validate reports, accept or return corrections, record the daily observation check, and sign the final report.

14
00:02:31,233 --> 00:02:35,969
The glossary lists every map color, from a row not yet started to a commissioned one.

15
00:02:37,467 --> 00:02:43,312
For questions or access permissions, contact Leonardo Dantas at C G N. Thank you!

